        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "This is pretty definitely going to be the podcast's crescendo...there's no way they topped it in only 4.5 more months of episodes.\n\n\"The final form of Nerd is Noel T\" - does that mean that all along he was actually Neltrd or Nerltd or Nlterd, but they just said it Nerd because there's No LT?\n\nGood without evil to oppose can easily still have motivation, but struggles to maintain a sense of urgency.  You can write stories with no conflict, but a professional writer is unlikely to meet deadline every month if there's no conflict driving him to crank out quick, easy stories of someone opposing someone or something else.  Making stories interesting without the easy crutch if antagonism is going to be harder and take longer, but I firmly believe it can be done.  I've enjoyed stories that have no conflict in them, it's not impossible, but it is probably a far more limited \"color space\" than if you add the extra shades of struggle.\n\n\"The stars can be their own torment\"...well, they certainly were for the Pepper Genie.",
